vt100 0.16.2, vendored
======================

Upstream: https://crates.io/crates/vt100/0.16.2 (https://github.com/doy/vt100-rust),
by Jesse Luehrs, MIT licensed (LICENSE, unchanged). The Terminal tab of Toolroll's
terminal workbench draws a take-over terminal through it (crates/toolroll-tui/src/term.rs).

Every file in src/ is upstream 0.16.2 byte for byte except grid.rs, row.rs and
screen.rs. Cargo.toml is ours: the package is named toolroll-vt100 (its library is
still `vt100`) and it is excluded from the workspace, so rustfmt and clippy leave
upstream's code as written.

Divergences
-----------

1. Faster scrolling (grid.rs `Grid::scroll_up`, row.rs).
   - A line scrolling inside a scroll region (or with no scrollback) rotates the
     region's rows and reuses the row that left the top as the new blank bottom
     row. Upstream allocated a new row and freed the old one for every line.
   - With a full scrollback, the oldest scrollback row is reused as the new blank
     row instead of being freed while another is allocated.
   - Row keeps `dirty`: every cell at or past it is blank (equal to Cell::new()).
     Writing a cell through get_mut, erase or clear_wide moves it out to cover that
     cell; insert, remove, a non-blank resize and a coloured clear mark the whole
     row. `Row::renew` (new) and a default-coloured `Row::clear` blank only the
     cells before `dirty`. Upstream filled every cell of every new row.
   Upstream held a 200-column pane to about 10 MB/s of short-line output (`yes`);
   this copy parses the same about seven times faster. Nothing drawn changes.

2. One-row and one-column screens (grid.rs `Grid::col_wrap`, screen.rs
   `Screen::text`). Upstream overflowed there and, built for release, then
   unwrapped a row or cell that doesn't exist (a crash a program's output could
   cause):
   - col_wrap compares `pos.col + width > cols` (upstream: `pos.col > cols - width`,
     which overflowed when a wide character met a one-column screen), and when
     the row a wrap left has scrolled away entirely (a one-row screen or region)
     it marks nothing, where upstream computed the index of a row above row 0.
   - text drops a wide character on a one-column screen, which can't hold it.
   The pane also never gives the emulator a screen under 2x2 (term.rs MIN_SIDE).
Every change carries a `toolroll` comment.

Checks: crates/toolroll-tui/tests/vt100_same.rs runs this copy and upstream 0.16.2
on the same bytes, split at the same places, and compares every cell, the cursor,
the formatted screen and every scrollback line, and checks that a reused row comes
back blank after every kind of write. It also runs this copy at 1x1, 1xN and Nx1
(upstream panics there, so those have no upstream to compare against).

Updating: take the new upstream release, reapply the three files' changes (search
for `toolroll`), and keep vt100_same.rs passing
against the new upstream version.
